# Partition layout for the Radxa ZERO 3E.
#
# Based on wic/generic-gptdisk.wks.in (this layer's default), with one
# change: the U-Boot proper partition moves from offset 2M to 8M.
#
# u-boot-radxa-zero3e (mainline-based U-Boot, see recipes-bsp/u-boot/
# u-boot-radxa-zero3e_2024.07.bb) uses a different SPL than the legacy
# u-boot-rockchip.bb this default layout was designed for: its SPL loads
# u-boot.itb from a *fixed raw sector* (not a GPT lookup by partition
# name), computed from CONFIG_SPL_PAD_TO=0x7f8000 in the board defconfig
# - i.e. sector 64 (where loader1/idbloader starts) + 0x7f8000/512
# sectors = sector 16384 = offset 8MiB. Leaving this at the default 2M
# puts u-boot.itb somewhere SPL never looks, so it fails with
# "mmc_load_image_raw_sector: mmc block read error" and never reaches
# U-Boot proper. This is exactly the offset the official upstream
# meta-rockchip layer's own wic/rockchip.wks uses for the same reason
# (its "loader2" partition sits at sector 16384 too).
#
# The "boot" partition is a real vfat filesystem with a generic
# U-Boot distro-boot extlinux.conf (auto-generated by the
# "bootimg-partition" wic source plugin from IMAGE_BOOT_FILES, see the
# machine conf), not a raw copy of the Rockchip-style boot.img -
# mainline U-Boot's autoboot (distro_bootcmd/bootstd, what
# u-boot-radxa-zero3e uses) only knows how to find a kernel via
# /extlinux/extlinux.conf on an actual filesystem partition; it has no
# way to load a raw Android-style boot.img. Without this, autoboot
# finds nothing on mmc and falls through to a network boot attempt.
#
# --active is required, not cosmetic: it sets the GPT "legacy_boot"
# attribute bit (wic runs `parted set <n> legacy_boot on` for GPT when
# this flag is given). U-Boot's bootdev_find_in_blk()
# (boot/bootdev-uclass.c) calls part_get_bootable() on the whole disk
# first; if it finds *no* partition with that bit set, it falls back to
# only ever scanning partition 1 and rejects every other partition with
# -EINVAL ("No partition found") *before* even checking for a
# filesystem - which is exactly what happened to partitions 2 (boot)
# and 3 (rootfs) without this flag, confirmed via
# `bootflow scan -lae` on the actual board.
#
# 0~32K: GPT
bootloader --ptable gpt --append="console=ttyFIQ0,1500000"
part --source rawcopy --sourceparams="file=idblock.img" --align 32 --no-table
part --source rawcopy --sourceparams="file=uboot.img" --part-name uboot --offset 8M
part --source rawcopy --sourceparams="file=trust.img" --part-name trust --align 4
part /boot --source bootimg-partition --sourceparams="loader=u-boot" --label boot --fstype=vfat --align 4 --fixed-size 64M --active --use-uuid
part / --source rootfs --fstype ${RK_ROOTFS_TYPE} --part-name rootfs --uuid ${RK_ROOTDEV_UUID} --mkfs-extraopts "${RK_ROOTFS_EXTRAOPTS}" --align 8192
